## 📍 AT A GLANCE — start here

**What this feature is:** let users browse & install curated MilkDrop preset packs from
inside DiscoCast, layered on top of the 1,144 bundled presets — installed packs play exactly
like the bundled ones.

**Where we are (2026-06-03):**
| | Phase | What | State |
|---|---|---|---|
| ✅ | **0** | Storage rebuild: custom presets localStorage → **IndexedDB** (kills the ~200-preset "Storage full" wall) | **SHIPPED & verified** — web + macOS |
| ✅ | **4** | **Tauri-FS mirror** — native-file preset storage on desktop (platform parity) | **BUILT** into a notarized macOS DMG · Windows needs its GH-Actions build (you trigger) |
| 📋 | **1** | **The import ENGINE** — community preset store + install/uninstall pipeline | **PLANNED & pick-up-ready (§13)** ← **NEXT** · no code yet |
| ⬜ | **2** | Manifest + "Browse Packs" UI — **design decided (§4): one shared tabbed modal** (`From File` + `Community Packs`); **progress UX specced (§2c): real % download + live "N / M installed" counts, inline per-card, cancellable, honest partial-success** | not started (design done) |
| ⬜ | **3** | `.milk` converter → ship curated **Cream-of-the-Crop** themed JSON packs | not started |

> Phase 4 ran ahead of 1–3 because it completed the **storage/parity foundation** (same track as
> Phase 0). The community-pack feature itself is Phases 1→2→3.

**▶️ NEXT SESSION:** build the engine — follow the ordered checklist in **§13.7**. First step:
confirm `jszip`, then add the community store to `presetStore.js`. Key design (verified, §13.1):
community presets register like **bundled** presets (raw JSON), **IndexedDB-only**, and **skip**
`refreshCustomPresets`.

**📦 Pack strategy (locked — §2.5):** ship **small, curated** themed packs; **AVOID the mega dumps**
(Ansorre 15k is unsorted + unlicensed; Cream 9.8k / WACUP 100k too big). The curated "best of" is
**Cream of the Crop** — convert one of its 11 themed categories at a time into a hosted drop-in JSON
pack (needs the Phase 3 converter).

**🗂 Where to read more:** §13 = the build plan · §11 = verified code audit · §2.5 = pack strategy ·
§5/§9 = storage architecture · §10 = full phase tracker (now superseded up here for status).

