## 0. Headline — The Storage Upgrade Is Phase 0 (and stands alone)

> 📜 _Historical context — Phase 0 is now SHIPPED & verified (see "At a Glance" up top). This
> section explains why it was the foundation; kept for the reasoning, not for current status._

**This is the part that matters even if community packs never ship.**

While planning pack import we found the real bottleneck isn't the packs — it's how
we store user presets *today*. The codebase audit (§11) verified it against the code:

- **Custom preset *metadata*** (baseVals / shapes / waves / warp / comp / frame_eqs /
  the images array) still lives in **localStorage** (`discocast_custom_presets`,
  [customPresets.js:11](src/customPresets.js#L11)). Image/video **blobs** already moved
  to IndexedDB / Tauri FS — so the 5–10 MB wall is on *metadata only*.
- That wall **already fails users**: `saveCustomPreset()` throws *"Storage full — export
  your presets to free space, then delete some"* on `QuotaExceededError`
  ([customPresets.js:56](src/customPresets.js#L56)). A power user with a few hundred
  layered presets hits it now.

### The fix — one unified IndexedDB preset-metadata store

Build **one** IndexedDB store for preset *metadata* and migrate **custom** presets onto
it first. This:

1. **Removes the ~200-preset wall for user-created presets** — ships real value with
   **zero** community-pack UI. This is the "needed even without this dev" upgrade.
2. **Becomes the substrate community packs plug into** — community presets are just the
   same store under a `community:<packId>:` namespace (§9.6). Build the foundation once.

### The insight that makes it safe — a boot-hydrated cache

The naïve "make storage async" plan ripples through **~15 synchronous readers** of
`loadAllCustomPresets()` across the editor + player (§11.3) and risks the engine's hot
paths. Instead:

> **Reads stay synchronous against an in-memory cache hydrated once at boot from
> IndexedDB. Only WRITES (save / delete) and the one-time localStorage→IDB migration go
> async.** The ~15 read sites keep working unchanged against the cache; only the 3–4
> write functions + boot hydration change.

This mirrors the **already-proven blob pattern** (`storeImage`/`getImage` route to
Tauri FS or IndexedDB transparently, [customPresets.js:175–204](src/customPresets.js#L175-L204)).

**Sequencing recommendation:** do Phase 0 (custom → unified IDB store, cache-backed)
first as a self-contained, shippable infra upgrade. Then community packs (§10 Phases 1–4)
plug into the same store. See the revised tracker in §10.

