## 2.5 Pack Strategy — small & curated, AVOID mega (user steer, 2026-06-02)

**Direction (locked):** stay away from the mega collections (Ansorre 15k, Cream 9.8k as a
whole, WACUP 100k, Archive 52k). Ship **small/medium, curated, drop-in packs that behave exactly
like our currently-bundled packs** (Butterchurn JSON, appear as normal presets, no conversion at
play time).

**The honest landscape after web verification (2026-06-02):** there is **no ready-made small +
curated + JSON + cleanly-licensed pack** out there. The two axes trade off:

| Tier | Examples | Drop-in JSON? | Curated/small? | Licensed? | Verdict |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Official Butterchurn JSON | Base/Extra/Extra2/MD1 + Baron | ✅ | — | ✅ MIT | **Already 100% bundled** — nothing left to add here |
| Pre-converted mega JSON | Ansorre 15k | ✅ | ❌ mega, unsorted | ⚠️ none | Avoid as product; OK as an engine smoke-test slice |
| **Curated `.milk`** | **Cream of the Crop** (11 themed categories, 5/5-rated, projectM default), Original MilkDrop ~400 | ❌ needs converter | ✅ **yes — per-category is small** | ✅ community/widely redistributed (verify) | **The real prize** — but needs the Phase 3 converter |

**Conclusion / recommended path:** the "best of" the user wants already exists — it's **Cream of
the Crop**, whose **11 category folders ARE the curated themed lists** (Dancer, Drawing, Fractal,
Geometric, Hypnotic, Particles, Reaction, Sparkle, Supernova, Waveform, Transition). The move is to
build the **.milk converter (Phase 3)** and convert **one category at a time** into clean,
small/medium **themed JSON packs we host** (e.g. "Geometric", "Waveform", "Sparkle" — a few hundred
each) — which then install and play *exactly* like the bundled packs. That delivers small + curated
+ drop-in (after a one-time, build-side conversion we do, not the user).

**Two-step plan that matches the steer:**
1. **Engine first (Phase 1):** build the community install pipeline; smoke-test it with a *small
   slice* of Ansorre JSON (e.g. 200–500 files) purely to prove drop-in install works. Throwaway.
2. **Curated product (Phase 3 + curation):** convert selected Cream-of-the-Crop categories → host
   as themed JSON packs in our manifest. These are the packs we actually ship to users.

> There is no good shortcut around the converter for *curated* content: essentially every
> hand-curated/best-of pack on the net is `.milk`. The only pre-converted JSON at scale is the
> unsorted, unlicensed Ansorre dump. So "small + curated + drop-in" = "we convert a Cream category
> ourselves, once."

