## 3. Technical Feasibility — Serving from GitHub

### How to get files from GitHub to the browser

| Method | CORS? | Rate limit | Best for |
|---|---|---|---|
| **jsDelivr CDN** | ✅ Yes | Generous (no hard limit) | Serving individual JSON files or ZIP archives. Production-grade CDN with permanent caching. |
| **GitHub Contents API** | ✅ Yes | 60/hr unauthenticated | Directory listings, file metadata. Too slow for 15k files. |
| **raw.githubusercontent.com** | ❌ No | - | Blocked by CORS in browsers. Not usable. |
| **GitHub Releases** | ✅ Via jsDelivr | - | Large ZIP archives. Best for mega-packs. |

### jsDelivr URL patterns (our delivery mechanism)

```
# Single file from a repo:
https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/{user}/{repo}@{branch}/{path}

# Example — one preset from Ansorre:
https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ansorre/tens-of-thousands-milkdrop-presets-for-butterchurn@master/milkdrop-presets-for-butterchurn.zip

# Example — Cream of the Crop readme/manifest:
https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/projectM-visualizer/presets-cream-of-the-crop@master/README.md

# Directory listing API:
https://data.jsdelivr.com/v1/packages/gh/{user}/{repo}
```

### Recommended approach: Curated manifest + jsDelivr delivery

Rather than querying GitHub APIs at runtime, we **host a static manifest** (JSON
file) that lists all available packs, their download URLs, and metadata. The app
fetches this manifest to populate the "Browse Packs" modal.

```jsonc
// Example manifest — SMALL CURATED PACKS ONLY (§2.5). Canonical schema lives in Phase 2a.
{
  "version": 1,
  "packs": [
    {
      "id": "cream-geometric",
      "name": "Cream — Geometric",
      "author": "Jason Fletcher (ISOSCELES)",
      "description": "~400 hand-curated Geometric presets (one Cream-of-the-Crop category)",
      "presetCount": 400,
      "format": "butterchurn-json-zip",   // we host pre-converted JSON
      "downloadUrl": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/<our-registry>/cream-geometric.zip",
      "sizeEstimate": "~4 MB",
      "rating": 5,
      "tags": ["curated", "geometric", "themed"]
    }
    // ... more small themed packs (Waveform, Sparkle, Classic MilkDrop, …)
  ]
}
```

**Benefits:**
- No GitHub API rate limits
- No CORS issues
- Manifest can be updated without app changes
- We control what's shown (curated, tested)
- Can add our own hosted packs later

