### Phase 0 — Unified IndexedDB Preset Store (the storage upgrade)

**Goal:** Move custom preset *metadata* off localStorage into a single IndexedDB store,
fronted by a boot-hydrated in-memory cache so existing synchronous readers don't change.
This removes the ~200-preset wall and becomes the substrate community packs reuse.

**Deliverables:**
```
NEW     src/presetStore.js     — the unified store: IDB metadata store + in-memory cache
MODIFY  src/customPresets.js   — route metadata CRUD through presetStore; keep the public
                                  sync read API (cache-backed) so callers don't change
```

**The cache contract (the core of why this is safe):**
```
Boot:   await presetStore.hydrate()   → reads ALL metadata from IDB into an in-memory map
Reads:  loadAllCustomPresets() / getCustomPreset(id)   → SYNC, served from the cache
                                                          (signatures unchanged)
Writes: saveCustomPreset() / createCustomPreset() / deleteCustomPreset()
          → update cache synchronously, then persist to IDB (async, fire-and-forget OK)
Migration (one-time, idempotent): on first boot, if localStorage `discocast_custom_presets`
          has records and IDB is empty → copy them into IDB, mark migrated, keep the
          localStorage copy as a backstop (don't delete until verified).
```

**Key design decisions:**
- **Metadata-only.** Blobs already live in IDB/Tauri FS (`storeImage`/`getImage`) — Phase 0
  does NOT touch them. Just the preset records that overflow localStorage today.
- **Same DB or a new one?** Recommend a dedicated DB `discocast_presets` (store `presets`,
  key = preset `id`) so it's independent of the `discocast_images` blob DB and of any
  future schema bump.
- **Boot ordering.** `hydrate()` must complete before the first `loadAllCustomPresets()`
  read. Audit the entry points (`main.js`, `editor/main.js`, `timeline/main.js`) — each
  must `await presetStore.hydrate()` before wiring the engine/inspector.
  **✅ VERIFIED FEASIBLE (2026-06-02) — do not re-investigate:** the player boot is already
  an `async` `DOMContentLoaded` handler that `await`s `initAuthGate()`, *then* constructs the
  engine, *then* calls `refreshCustomPresets()` (the first preset read) at
  [main.js:38](src/main.js#L38). So `await presetStore.hydrate()` drops in as a single line
  immediately before line 38 — the cache is populated before any read, no race, no surgery.
  The editor (`editor/main.js`) and timeline (`timeline/main.js`) follow the same async-boot
  pattern; add the same one line. This is the assumption the whole "reads stay sync" design
  rests on, and it holds.
- **Tauri.** WKWebView IndexedDB can be evicted under storage pressure (same risk noted for
  blobs). Phase 4 adds the Tauri-FS mirror for metadata; Phase 0 ships IDB-only (matches
  how blobs shipped before their Tauri fallback).

**Call sites that change (from §11.3):**
- Writers (must update cache + IDB): `inspector.js:9923/9925` (save/create),
  `presetLibrary.js:350` (delete), `controls.js:713` (delete).
- Readers (UNCHANGED — served by cache): `presetRegistry.js:25`, `visualizer.js:577`,
  `controls.js:703/732/743/762`, `editor/main.js:160/555`, `presetLibrary.js:146/168/310/349`.
- Boot: add `await presetStore.hydrate()` in the three `main.js` entry points.

**Verification (0c):**
- Programmatically create 500 custom presets → confirm no QuotaExceededError, all persist
  across reload, drawer + Library list + timeline all show them.
- Confirm a pre-Phase-0 user (records only in localStorage) auto-migrates on first boot and
  loses nothing.
- Confirm editor save/load/delete + player drawer + timeline all still work (the cache must
  be byte-identical to the old localStorage read path).

