#### Phase 0 — VERIFIED EXECUTION TRACE & FILE-BY-FILE BUILD SPEC (2026-06-02)

This is the written save/load-flow trace CLAUDE.md mandates before code. Every path below was
read in the actual source, not inferred.

**Save flow as it exists today (real path):**
```
Studio "Save" → editor/main.js attemptSave() (L553) reads loadAllCustomPresets() to check
                name collision → inspector.saveCurrent(name, id) (inspector.js:9900)
  → builds `data = { name, ...currentState, solidColor, thumbnailDataUrl? }`
  → id present?  saveCustomPreset({...data, id, updatedAt}) (inspector.js:9923)
     else        createCustomPreset(data) (inspector.js:9925)
  → customPresets.js: saveCustomPreset() reads localStorage, merges, JSON.stringify→setItem
     (THROWS friendly "Storage full" on QuotaExceededError, L56)
```
**Load flow:** `editor/main.js:160` `loadAllCustomPresets()[id]` → `inspector.loadPresetData()`.
Player: `controls.js` → `engine.refreshCustomPresets()` (reads localStorage) → drawer.
**Delete flow:** Studio `presetLibrary.js:350` / player `controls.js:713` → `deleteCustomPreset(id)`
+ blob cleanup via `deleteImage()`. **Rename flow:** `presetLibrary.js:308 commit()` → RAW
`localStorage.setItem` (the §11.3 trap).

**Design: `customPresets.js` keeps its exact public API; a cache backs it.** Callers don't change
(except the rename refactor). The localStorage read/write *inside* the API functions is swapped
for cache reads + async IDB persistence.

**File-by-file changes:**

```
NEW  src/presetStore.js
     • openDB()            → IndexedDB `discocast_presets`, store `presets` (key = id)
     • hydrate()           → async; loads ALL records into module-level `_cache` Map.
                             One-time migration: if localStorage `discocast_custom_presets`
                             (or legacy `milkscreen_custom_presets`) has records AND the IDB
                             store is empty → copy them in, set a `__dc_presets_migrated` flag,
                             KEEP localStorage as a backstop (do NOT delete in Phase 0).
     • getAllSync()        → returns `{ [id]: record }` from cache (sync)
     • getOneSync(id)      → cache.get(id) (sync)
     • putAsync(record)    → cache.set + async IDB put; on IDB quota error, surface same
                             "Storage full" message (defensive — IDB quota is huge, unlikely)
     • deleteAsync(id)     → cache.delete + async IDB delete
     • isHydrated()        → guard so a read before hydrate() throws a clear dev error

MOD  src/customPresets.js
     • loadAllCustomPresets()  → return presetStore.getAllSync()   (was localStorage.getItem+parse)
     • getCustomPreset(id)     → presetStore.getOneSync(id)
     • saveCustomPreset(p)     → build record (unchanged), presetStore.putAsync(record), return record
     • deleteCustomPreset(id)  → presetStore.deleteAsync(id)
     • (export a `hydratePresets = presetStore.hydrate` passthrough so entry points import one module)

MOD  src/editor/presetLibrary.js
     • L308–319 commit(): replace the raw localStorage.setItem block with
       `saveCustomPreset({ ...all[id], name: next, updatedAt: Date.now() })` inside the existing
       try/catch (keeps the "Storage full" toast).

MOD  src/main.js            → add `await hydratePresets()` immediately before
                              `engine.refreshCustomPresets()` (L38). VERIFIED feasible (Phase 0c note).
MOD  src/editor/main.js     → add `await hydratePresets()` in the async DOMContentLoaded boot,
                              before the first loadAllCustomPresets()/inspector wiring.
MOD  src/timeline/main.js   → same one-line hydrate before `engine.refreshCustomPresets()` (L209).
```

**Invariants this must preserve (the burn-list):**
- The public API **signatures are unchanged** → the ~15 readers (§11.3) are not touched.
- `saveCustomPreset` still **returns the record synchronously** (callers use the return value
  immediately — e.g. `inspector.saveCurrent` returns it). The cache update is sync; only the IDB
  write is deferred. So the return contract holds.
- The **"Storage full" message survives** (now on the IDB-quota path + the rename toast).
- **No data loss on migration** → localStorage retained as backstop until 0c signs off; migration
  is idempotent (flag-guarded, only runs when IDB is empty).
- **Blob cleanup on delete is untouched** — `deleteImage()` calls in `controls.js`/`presetLibrary.js`
  stay exactly as-is; Phase 0 is metadata-only.

**Out of scope for Phase 0 (do NOT do here):** community namespace (Phase 1a), Tauri-FS metadata
mirror (Phase 4), deleting the localStorage backstop (a later cleanup once IDB is trusted in prod).

