### Phase 4 — Polish

#### Phase 4 — Tauri-FS metadata mirror (CONCRETE SPEC, 2026-06-02)

**What it is:** make preset *metadata* survive on the desktop app even if WKWebView evicts
IndexedDB under disk pressure, by persisting records to the native filesystem (app data dir) —
the same way blobs already do. **Web/Windows-web are untouched** (no `window.__TAURI__`).

**Why the pattern is low-risk:** the Rust + JS plumbing already exists for blobs and is proven.
`store_blob`/`get_blob`/`delete_blob` ([src-tauri/src/main.rs:164–210](src-tauri/src/main.rs#L164-L210))
write base64 files under `app_data_dir()/images/`; `customPresets.js` routes to them when
`window.__TAURI__` is present. The metadata mirror is the same shape, one directory over.

**Rust (src-tauri/src/main.rs) — ~3 commands, ~40 lines, modelled on store_blob:**
```
store_preset(app, id, json)   → write app_data_dir/presets/<id>.json   (json is plain text, not base64)
get_all_presets(app)          → read app_data_dir/presets/*.json → Vec<String>  (hydrate source on desktop)
delete_preset(app, id)        → remove app_data_dir/presets/<id>.json
```
…then add the three names to `tauri::generate_handler![ … ]` (main.rs:374).

**JS (src/presetStore.js) — add a `window.__TAURI__` branch:**
- `hydrate()`: on Tauri, the **filesystem is authoritative** (IDB can be evicted) — read
  `get_all_presets` into the cache. One-time migrate IDB→FS the first run (write each record).
- `putRecord()` / `deleteRecord()`: on Tauri, also `invoke('store_preset' / 'delete_preset')`.
- Keep the in-memory cache exactly as today, so the sync read API is unchanged on every platform.

**Open design decision (the only real thinking):** on desktop, FS-authoritative vs FS-as-backup.
Recommendation: **FS-authoritative on Tauri** (that's the whole point — eviction-proof). The IDB
copy becomes a redundant cache. Mirror, don't dual-source-of-truth.

**Verification cost — this is why it's NOT a dev-server task:** `window.__TAURI__` only exists in
the packaged/`tauri dev` app, so it **cannot be tested in `npm run dev`**. Proving it needs a Tauri
build — and per README, the real build is **`./build-and-sign.sh`** (Vite + Tauri compile + sign +
Apple notarize + DMG), a ~10–15 min, network/Apple-dependent process that streams live and must not
be backgrounded. That is a different, heavier workflow than the JS-only iteration Phase 0 used.

**Recommendation on timing (2026-06-02):** **defer.** Phase 0 on IndexedDB already works in the
desktop app today; eviction is an unobserved risk, not a current failure. The localStorage backstop
(Phase 0d, kept) covers pre-migration presets in the meantime. Do this mirror as its own focused
session — ideally bundled with the *next* macOS build you ship anyway, or the moment eviction is
ever actually observed. Don't stack a Rust change + a notarized build on top of still-uncommitted
Phase 0 JS.

**Community-pack note (the original Phase 4 bullet):** the same mechanism stores community preset
JSONs under `app_data_dir/community/<packId>/` — but that only matters once Phase 1+ ships, and a
15k-pack on the FS is a separate scale question. Custom-preset metadata is the first/only thing that
needs this today.

##### ✅ WHAT SHIPPED (2026-06-02 — metadata mirror built into a notarized DMG)

- **Rust** ([src-tauri/src/main.rs](src-tauri/src/main.rs)): added `store_preset(id, json)` /
  `get_all_presets()` / `delete_preset(id)` (modelled on `store_blob`), writing
  `app_data_dir/presets/<id>.json` as plain UTF-8; registered all three in `generate_handler!`.
  `cargo check` ✓.
- **JS** ([src/presetStore.js](src/presetStore.js)): `_isTauri()` branch. On desktop the **FS is
  authoritative** — `hydrate()` reads `get_all_presets`; first run with an empty FS migrates from
  the best source (IndexedDB from Phase 0, else the localStorage snapshot) and writes each to disk
  (IDB + localStorage left intact as backstops). `putRecord`/`deleteRecord` invoke
  `store_preset`/`delete_preset`. Web/Windows-web unchanged (no `window.__TAURI__`) → IndexedDB path.
- **Build:** full `./build-and-sign.sh` → app + DMG both **notarized: Accepted**, stapled,
  `source=Notarized Developer ID`. Output: `promo/DiscoCast Visualizer-1.0.20260602.2005.dmg`
  (+ canonical `promo/DiscoCast-Visualizer.dmg`). Real bundle id = **`app.discocast.visualizer`**.

**🔬 In-app runtime test still pending (the one thing the build can't prove):** install the DMG,
save/rename/delete a preset, then confirm files appear/update/disappear in
`~/Library/Application Support/app.discocast.visualizer/presets/`, and that they survive an app
relaunch. Also confirm a pre-existing desktop user's presets migrate IDB→FS on first launch.

**Known edge (logged, not blocking):** if the first-run IDB→FS migration write fails partway, the
next launch sees a non-empty FS and won't re-migrate the missing ones — but IDB + localStorage are
retained as backstops, so nothing is lost; a future reconcile pass can close this.

**Committed + pushed to `main` 2026-06-02** (`353735e` source + `da26f05` DMG; Phase 0 itself was
`cbdc54a`). Web/promo auto-deploy via Coolify. **Windows build triggered** via GitHub Actions
("Build Windows Installer", run 26856188495) so a fresh `.exe` with the new Rust commands is ready
for shadow.tech testing.

##### Cross-platform matrix — which storage path each target uses

| Target | `window.__TAURI__`? | Storage path | Needs a fresh build for today's mirror? |
|---|---|---|---|
| Web (browser / Coolify) | no | IndexedDB (Phase 0) | No — JS-only; ships on next web deploy |
| Dev server (`localhost:5173`) | no | IndexedDB | No (but it therefore does NOT exercise the FS mirror) |
| **macOS app** (Tauri/WKWebView) | yes | **native FS** (`store_preset`) | ✅ Done — in the 2026-06-02 notarized DMG |
| **Windows app** (Tauri/WebView2) | **yes** | **native FS** (`store_preset`) | ⚠️ **YES — must rebuild via GitHub Actions** |

**Windows gotcha (important):** the Windows desktop app is *also* Tauri, so `presetStore.js` takes
the `_isTauri()` FS branch there too — it will call `store_preset`/`get_all_presets`/`delete_preset`.
The **existing/old Windows `.exe` does not contain those Rust commands** (built before today), so a
fresh **GitHub Actions Windows build** (which compiles the new Rust + JS together) is required before
Windows persistence works. The FS path itself is cross-platform — `app_data_dir()` resolves to
`%APPDATA%\app.discocast.visualizer\presets\` on Windows automatically. Test target = shadow.tech.

**Order of operations for Windows test:** commit + push → trigger "Build Windows Installer" Action →
install that `.exe` on shadow.tech → verify save/relaunch persistence + the `presets\` folder.

#### Other Phase 4 polish

- **Tauri FS fallback (community packs):** Store community preset JSONs in
  `~/Library/Application Support/app.discocast.visualizer/community/` alongside
  IndexedDB. Mirror the `_storeImageTauri` / `_getImageTauri` pattern from
  `customPresets.js`.
- **Deduplication:** Skip community presets whose names match bundled ones (by
  display name, case-insensitive). Or auto-prefix: "cream-geometric: Preset Name".
- **User Guide:** Add "Community Packs" section to help modal (index.html + help.html).
- **Pack update detection:** Compare manifest `version` field with stored
  `installedAt` to show "Update available" badge.
- **Drawer UI:** Add a "Community" tab or a section divider in the drawer so
  users can filter/search community presets separately.

